<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giacomo IV Crispo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1520">1520</a>–<a href="/years/1576">1576</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as James IV Crispo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giacomo IV Crispo was the last Duke of Naxos, ruler of the Duchy of the Archipelago in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyclades">Cyclades</a> from 1564. The duchy had long been an Ottoman tributary, and in 1566 his Greek subjects complained of his misrule, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Selim II deposed him. The islands were given to the Jewish financier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-nasi">Joseph Nasi</a>, ending more than three and a half centuries of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> rule in Naxos.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giacomo-iv-crispo.jpg" alt="Giacomo IV Crispo" width="296" height="371" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Muriel Pécastaing-Boissière · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crispi_Coat_of_Arms.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
